["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"aep","stream_identity":"01a0cae6-7e88-710c-8913-d70d29cb7b4c","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIG68b0d7d02b4d508cbfe06d62d2f75bb44b99a812d5ab534ee59423399c8eb3ed","locator":"ep://planning/store/task/planning-migration-raw-capture-values","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":10,"type":"aep.task/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Context\n\nThis is a bounded implementation task within story:eventlog-planning-authority-migration, not a\nsecond migration owner. Existing coordinates are modeled in specs/planning-migration/. The accepted\npure transport contract is docs/design/planning-raw-capture-v0.1.md, digest\na4f5d1d3f8a1e75130eb5ebe8ee30d0ecc613c390eb061d8015a3b9a0230105a.\nTwo independent design reviews completed. The second remains needs-revision; the coordinator fixed\nits hybrid-policy omission afterward and accepted bounded implementation without claiming independent\napproval of that correction. All six findings have recorded fixed outcomes on the owner story.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nThe IO-free Rust 1.85 aep-contract migration API preserves, validates and deterministically hashes\nevery closed raw-capture outcome described by the accepted contract, with matching generated schema,\nindependent byte-vector and mutation tests, and passing affected suites, strict Clippy and MSRV checks.\n\n## Required evidence\n\nExercise every enum envelope and required field, raw host-path preservation and host-independent\nadmission, every method phase roster and refusal prefix, partial catalog/row retention, exact capture\nreconstruction and unstable differences, all 48 hybrid policies and missing/contradictory policy\ncontrols, exact transcript/snapshot/evidence framing and ordering. Expected vector bytes are literals;\nthe implementation must not calculate its own expected answers. Preserve existing schema bytes and\npure library compiler minimum. Full task check and independent code examination remain prerequisites\nto integration. No test result or schema has yet been produced by this task.\n\n## Scope\n\n- crates/plan/aep-contract/src/migration/ — inferred; new pure Rust values, validators, digest and tests.\n- crates/plan/aep-contract/src/lib.rs — cited; public module export.\n- crates/plan/aep-contract/Cargo.toml — cited; narrowly necessary SHA dependency and test dependencies.\n- crates/edge/aep-schema/Cargo.toml — cited; direct contract dependency.\n- crates/edge/aep-schema/src/schema.rs — cited; RawCaptureObservation schema roster and its tests.\n- schemas/generated/ — cited; generated only by cargo xtask schema, preserving all existing bytes.\n- Cargo.lock — cited; only changes required by the above wiring, no runtime pin or broad MSRV change.\n- CHANGELOG.md — cited; coordinator-owned Unreleased record before integration.\n\n## Remaining owner obligations\n\nActual catalog queries, source acquisition, writer control, semantic/history import, qualified\nER/Eventlog runtime, command/report binding and all six real cutovers remain under the same story.\nThe recorded runtime dependency blocker stays open. No physical writer facts are required to build\nthese pure values; their hashes do not prove IO isolation, authenticity, a receipt or a writer fence.\n\n## First executable regression\n\nThe unchanged aep-schema baseline executed 28 unit and 8 integration tests successfully, zero\nfailures or ignored cases, exit0. Adding only the required raw-capture schema roster expectation\nthen executed 27 passing and one failing unit test, exit101, with the exact failure\n`raw-capture-observation.schema.json is not published`. Production implementation had not begun.\nThe same locked/offline Rust1.98.1 package command produced both results. Doctest count was zero\non baseline;