ol, semantic import, runtime migration or real cutover has been\nimplemented by this pure-value task. The single parent migration owner remains open.\n\n## Four reproduced source findings corrected\n\nFirst source examination review-result:raw-capture-code-pass-1 remains immutable, original report\nSHA589c069a0df94df03c69253cf785ee1b19874dcf153dc3dff316a5857e3a1d59. Three blockers and one\ndiagnostic-accumulation warning were reproduced by public-input integration tests. A separate fixed\ncorrection assignment is now CLOSED; its source changes only capture.rs and own lease is released.\n\n| First-review site | Outcome | Exact evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| capture.rs:1396 known preflight source compatibility | fixed | correction0001green; guard revert0010exit101; restoration0011exit0 |\n| capture.rs:2658 unresolved/unreachable root coordinates | fixed | correction0002green; guard revert0012exit101; restoration0013exit0 |\n| capture.rs:1837 retained foreign-node exact refusal | fixed | correction0003green; guard revert0014exit101; restoration0015exit0 |\n| capture.rs:1300 accumulated supplied-capture defects | fixed | correction0004green; guard revert0016exit101; restoration0017exit0 |\n\nAll evidence is under local-evidence:ess-evolution/waves/0005-aep-migration/raw-capture-correction-1/.\nOriginal author report13e87655356a84a368b11c6aef8b151a77f950c08ae99086bc231a1ea8debe63 and\nmanifested raw command/log/exits remain unchanged. Rust1.98.1 and actualRust1.85 affected suites,\nstrict Clippy, schema-check and source rustfmt pass; restored final four-case suite exits0.\nProduction capture.rs SHA21af3eb10d881ee4053c57b397cf26efd8bf1ea66e666eefea34e7e22891bc10.\n\nRoot applied rustfmt only to the adopted independent test after its original formatting was found\nnot gate-clean. The retained original9595c577… remains in review1. Exact before/after diff changes\nonly two expression layouts, with no assertion change. Formatted test SHA\n45565b05cdc28324b6dc4c9aa7566de0279d0ec5a31c49eb0464edba71ef78b9; root ran all4cases again,\ncoordinator-formatted-regressions.exit0, and source/test scoped rustfmt0.\n\nCorrected local bot submission b3e29e4fab23a62d3d0e2de433f12322573548ce (47966/46081e exit0)\ncontains exactly capture.rs, the four retained regressions and a CHANGELOG entry. No publication or\nintegration. The remaining second and final source examination covers this submission against\noriginal pure base4eb999e0ae3cc77d1c387152e23a85ad4eae86dc. Review budget is not reset. Full\nrepository task check and migration command/runtime/cutover acceptance remain required.\n\n## Final source examination and pending-batch correction\n\nThe immutable final report review-result:raw-capture-code-pass-2 examines submitted\nb3e29e4fab23a62d3d0e2de433f12322573548ce. Its trend resolves all four earlier findings and introduces\none pending-batch classification blocker. No third source examination is scheduled.\n\nThe separately bounded final correction now selects PendingBatchPresent for an exact root regular\n.aep-batch.pending.json node using Unix bytes or Windows UTF-16 units. Other foreign regular files,\nsymlinks and other nodes retain ForeignMarkdownNode; coordinates remain exact. Root examined the\nproduction diff and all companion assertions and verified the original reviewer test unchanged.\nFinal capture source SHA-256 61b548113667a03fcbda7b6a20b805a436df68c752e81bea88e499161c13bfc4.\nOriginal reviewer test SHA-256 ebaf3dbe33822aa2ce3d55a570e81c8cc2833c42644962313bfcc4e137ee5c11;\nprior four-case test retains 45565b05cdc28324b6dc4c9aa7566de0279d0ec5a31c49eb0464edba71ef78b9.\n\nOriginal regression compiled and failed before the correction, passed afterward; reverting only\nthe correction restored that failure and restoration passed. Unix/Windows, wrong-code and nested-\nlookalike companions pass. Actual Rust1.98.1 and Rust1.85 complete suites each execute58contract\nand38schema cases; strict all-target Clippy and scoped formatting pass. An initial Clippy failure\nfor identical match arms was corrected without changing the behavior. Worker assignment is closed,\nits lease/token released. No SQL/provider or acquisition work was included.\n\nEvidence: local-evidence:ess-evolution/waves/0005-aep-migration/raw-capture-final-correction/report.md,\nSHA-256 6a6eada9c504dd4637b528076f5a1f6591bfb99ec4817bcedeac80cde276b743, with per-command raw\nlogs/exits. Root observations2331e1/4771cd/2095f3 and c6ff66 verify source, original regression,\ncompanion class, actual suite and mutation output. The finding is fixed, not independently reapproved.\nActual full AEP task check and local integration remain required. Migration commands remain open.\n\n## Actual full-gate attempt and bounded planning correction\n\nThe actual repository task check on local source commit\n715e52a88df9abcfcdd35752c09ab64b1e5a3fb3 exited201. The complete before/after nonignored source\nmanifest compared equal (exit0). The gate passed its steps through strict Clippy and stopped\nduring workspace tests: two existing xtask scope tests found the same nonexistent future backend\ncrate in the parent story's draft scope. Later gate steps are unexecuted, including PostgreSQL,\ndocumentation, MSRV and website; no whole-gate acceptance is claimed.\n\nRoot corrected only the parent story's scope through AEP, retaining the planned backend in prose\nand its already-scoped Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock creation surfaces. AEP validation passes with retained\nhistorical notices. The unchanged compiled scope-test binary now passes all five cases. No source\nguard or assertion was changed and neither closed source examination is reopened. The complete\ngate still must pass against a fresh source manifest before this pure task can be accepted.\n\nExact local evidence: local-evidence:ess-evolution/waves/0005-aep-migration/raw-capture-full-gate/.\nThe existing disposable PostgreSQL fixture is retained for the required actual backend lane.\nThe parent migration command and all real-store cutover requirements remain unimplemented.\n\n## Verified pure capture implementation\n\nThe bounded pure raw-capture deliverable is implemented and verified at local bot source commit\n715e52a88df9abcfcdd35752c09ab64b1e5a3fb3. Both source examinations are closed; the final introduced\npending-marker classification finding is corrected and its original regression is preserved.\nNo third examination was added.\n\nActual complete task check passed with exit0, source comparison0 and manifest generation0.\nAll16 steps executed, including real disposable PostgreSQL integration, Rust1.85 workspace build\nand website npm ci/build. Full log SHA8c4c9b12777cd5ddc41b0e969e6ceaf200936cf223787022036ba95876c41e23;\nall1094 before/after source files agree under manifest\ne95e15003be9e6c04abb5d7767178ec819569b1bec12b4748a0f4ceda52b2458.\nThe previous full-gate scope failure, CLI-only correction and successful unchanged guard remain\nrecorded. Signed common evidence also passed for the committed source; no required gate was replaced.\n\nExact local evidence: local-evidence:ess-evolution/waves/0005-aep-migration/raw-capture-full-gate/acceptance.md\nand retry-after-scope/task-check.log. This closes only the finite pure task. The single parent\nmigration owner still owes acquisition, semantic imports, configuration, durable commands, qualified\nER/Eventlog integration, demonstrated writer control and all six actual store cutovers.\n","relations":[{"decomposes":"story:eventlog-planning-authority-migration"},{"serves":"vision:O2"}],"status":"implemented","title":"Implement pure planning migration raw capture values and digests"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIG68b0d7d02b4d508cbfe06d62d2f75bb44b99a812d5ab534ee59423399c8eb3ed","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":10,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIG68b0d7d02b4d508cbfe06d62d2f75bb44b99a812d5ab534ee59423399c8eb3ed"]}]